## Core v0.1-v0.2.1 (current research consolidation)
- IEPP renamed and narrowed to Individual Entity Proof Protocol
- canonical continuation separated from metaphysical originality
- TRP 2.0 reframed as a capability-indexed Canonical Continuation Game
- authenticated predecessor-bound transitions and atomic single-successor acceptance implemented
- predictable-entropy, key-plus-state, registry-split, and statistical-separation negative controls made mandatory
- L1 single-registry evidence boundary and F00-F12 single-host durability limits documented
- entropy-field ablation confirmed that tested L1 serialization comes from freshness, predecessor agreement, signatures, and atomic head update rather than entropy
- public title, citation metadata, README, and manuscript aligned to policy-relative canonical continuation
- arXiv manuscript and reproducibility package prepared for independent review

